------------------------            MODULES            ------------------------

formats.py
	Module containing functions for dealing with I/O and specific formats
	Includes GFF & TSV parsers, among other stuff

libintrons.py
	Module containing code for dealing with intron scoring & selection
	Chiefly includes the GenomicSequence class (& subclasses), as well as
	functions for deserializing GFF files to GenomicSequence subclasses and
	scoring	introns
	Itself import formats.py

extras.py
	Module containing one-off functions for various bespoke operations



------------------------            SCRIPTS            ------------------------

add_attrib.py
	Given a GFF, the name of an attribute & a TSV file listing
	feature IDs and attribute values, create/overwrite the atribute with
	the given value for each listed feature

add_introns.py
	Given a GFF, interpose introns between each pair of exons
	If the GFF's referened FASTA is supplied, the introns will have their
	splice sites denoted under the "splice_site" attribute

apply_adoptions.py
	Given the output of prepare_adoptions.py and a GFF, apply the adoptions
	listed

count_children.py
	Given a GFF, count how many children each contained feature has

del_attrib.py
	Given a GFF, the name of an attribute & a list of feature IDs, remove
	the given attribute from listed entries

enumerate_frags.py
	Given a GFF, generate IDs for exons & introns which are based on their
	order within the gene

extract_attrib.py
	Given a GFF and the name of an attribute, extract and list the value of
	that attribute for every feature which has that attribute

find_altseq_fa.py
	Given a FASTA, find pairs of sequences which may originate from the
	same sequenced transcript

find_altseq_gff.py
	Given a GFF+FASTA, find pairs of transcript mapping which may originate
	from the same sequenced transcript
	By default, each unique pair of transcript mappings is checked; pass
	the output of group_features.py to only compare mappings if they
	overlap

find_mrna_mismatches.py
	Given a transcriptome-to-genome mapping GFF, a genome FASTA and a
	transcriptome FASTA, find mappings whose sequences do not match the
	original transcript sequence

get_ft_len.py
	Given a GFF, report the length of each feature

get_orf_len.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, report the length of each transcript's longest ORF

group_by_parent.py
	Given a GFF, group features such that children of the same parent belong in
	the same group

group_features.py
	Given a GFF, group features based on if they overlap one another

introns_corn.py
	Given a GFF, mark each intron possessing a "splice_site" attribute as
	conventional or nonconventional, based on the splice site sequence

list_by_type.py
	Given a GFF & a list of type(s), list all features of the given types

prepare_adoptions.py
	Given the output of find_altseq_gff.py and the output of get_ft_len.py,
	determine which transcript mappings collectively originate from the
	same sequenced transcript, and find the most representative mapping
	for each group
	Based on this, prepare a file describing adoptions, to serve as input
	for apply_adoptions.py

rectify_introns.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, find and score all intron variants, then select
	the  variant for each intron

rectify_strand.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA and several data files, apply corrections to the GFF's
	strand information

rename_attr.py
	Given a GFF, the current name of an attribute, and a new name of the
	attribute, rename that attribute in all entries

rename_type.py
	Given a GFF, the current name of a type, and a new name of the type,
	rename that type for all relevant entries

set_ft_type.py
	Given a GFF, a list of feature IDs and the name of a feature type, replace
	the listed features' type with the given type

split_gff.py
	Given a GFF & a list of feature IDs, create two files - one containing all
	listed features, along with their lineages, and one excluding all listed
	features, along with as much of their lineages as possible

subset_gff.py
	Given a GFF & a list of feature IDs, subset the GFF file to
	exclude/include	the listed features and all of their children
	Assumes every feature in the GFF with a Parent attribute comes after
	its parent

undo_gmap_dir.py
	Given a GFF output by GMAP, undo its strand rectification

xchg_attrs.py
	Given a GFF & two attribute names, swap their values in all entries